# text = Upon its surface of bronze were elaborately wrought , in the still exquisite workmanship of Greece , reliefs of the Olympian games ; the two horses that drew the car were of the rarest breed of Parthia ; their slender limbs seemed to disdain the ground and court the air , and yet at the slightest touch of the charioteer , who stood behind the young owner of the equipage , they paused motionless , as if suddenly transformed into stone -- lifeless , but lifelike , as one of the breathing wonders of Praxiteles .
