# text = At the extremity of the hall , on either side to the right and left , if the house is large , there are two small recesses , rather than chambers , generally devoted to the ladies of the mansion ; and in the centre of the tessellated pavement of the hall is invariably a square , shallow reservoir for rain water ( classically termed impluvium ), which was admitted by an aperture in the roof above ; the said aperture being covered at will by an awning .
