# text = When the poet is your host , his verses are sure to charm said Lepidus said Clodius , ironically at heart , though not in appearance said Glaucus , in a soft voice said Lepidus , conceitedly said Pansa said Clodius sighed the umbra said Glaucus began Lepidus cried Clodius muttered the coxcomb to himself , as he fell back disdainfully on his couch said Clodius said Glaucus echoed Glaucus said the umbra cried Glaucus added he , once more rattling the dice said the complaisant Glaucus Lepidus and Sallust played at odd and even , and the umbra looked on , while Glaucus and Clodius became gradually absorbed in the chances of the dice cried Glaucus , ' this is the second time I have thrown the caniculae ' ( the lowest throw said Clodius , rattling the box for several moments as he threw the highest cast , named from that goddess -- whom he who wins money , indeed , usually propitiates said Glaucus , gaily whispered Lepidus replied Sallust , in the same tone said Glaucus began Clodius groaned the umbra exclaimed Glaucus
