# text = The young man lifted up his head , and gazed with a vacant and wondering stare upon the Egyptian continued Arbaces , in an earnest and solemn voice , casting first his searching eyes around to see that they were still alone Apaecides remained silent , but the changes rapidly passing over his speaking countenance betrayed the effect produced upon him by the words of the Egyptian -- words made tenfold more eloquent by the voice , the aspect , and the manner of the man resumed Arbaces Apaecides groaned aloud .
