# text = Arbaces , pausing for a moment , gazed on the pair with a brow from which all the usual stern serenity had fled ; he recovered himself by an effort , and slowly approached them , but with a step so soft and echoless , that even the attendants heard him not ; much less Ione and her lover said Glaucus Both started , and recognized behind the seat of Ione the cold and sarcastic face of the Egyptian said Glaucus , rising , and with a forced smile returned Arbaces , seating himself , and motioning to Glaucus to do the same said Ione replied the Egyptian
