# text = When the bark sails on over the smoothest wave , the fable tells us of the diminutive fish that can cling to the keel and arrest its progress : so is it ever with the great passions of mankind ; and we should paint life but ill if , even in times the most prodigal of romance , and of the romance of which we most largely avail ourselves , we did not also describe the mechanism of those trivial and household springs of mischief which we see every day at work in our chambers and at our hearths .
