# text = Nydia started as by a sudden impulse from the wall against which she had leaned : she threw herself at the feet of Stratonice ; she embraced her knees , and looking up at her with those sightless but touching eyes sobbed she said the hag , dragging her up rudely by one of those delicate hands , fit for no harsher labor than that of weaving the flowers which made her pleasure or her trade said Burbo , drawing forth his purse , and chinking its contents said Stratonice , nodding to Calenus cried Nydia , casting her eyes round the apartment with so fearful and straining a survey , that Calenus rose in alarm from his seat muttered he said she ; and she again burst into tears said Burbo , impatiently said Stratonice , pushing the poor child by the shoulders .
