# text = The gladiator , with a significant glance at his companions , extended an arm which , if not so huge in its girth as those of his comrades , was so firm in its muscles , so beautifully symmetrical in its proportions , that the three visitors uttered simultaneously an admiring exclamation said Clodius , tablet in hand returned Tetraides , sharply , and with an envious scowl cried Glaucus said Lydon returned Lydon , proudly said Clodius ; shall it be , Lepidus ?-- even betting , with swords said Clodius Clodius wrote the bet in his book said Lydon , in a low voice to Glaucus A blush mantled over the bronzed cheek of the gladiator said Lydon , haughtily , and he withdrew to the other end of the room cried Clodius said Niger , pointing to the door at the extremity of the room quoth Lepidus cried Lepidus , laughing At this moment a loud cry of pain and terror startled the group exclaimed Glaucus , and he darted at once into the quarter whence the cry rose .
