# text = The slave , wondering and grumbling , cast round his heavy eyes , and before one of the altars , whose remains still crowd the narrow space , he beheld a form bending as in meditation cried Nydia said a low and melancholy voice replied the priest , emerging from the altar , and approaching the rail Waving her hand to the slave , she bade him withdraw to a distance ; and he , who naturally imagined some superstition connected , perhaps , with the safety of Ione , could alone lead her to the temple , obeyed , and seated himself on the ground , at a little distance said she , speaking quick and low answered Nydia said Apaecides , fearfully cried the priest , passing his wan hand over his brow said Apaecides , retiring into one of the cells that flank the temple , and reappearing in a few moments wrapped in a large cloak , which was then much worn by all classes , and which concealed his sacred dress he said , grinding his teeth Muttering these disconnected thoughts , Apaecides , followed by his silent and sightless companion , hastened through the most solitary paths to the house of the Egyptian .
