# text = Half incredulous , half believing , half awed , half alarmed by the words of her strange host , she remained for some moments silent , and then answered Again the heart of Ione murmured ' Glaucus' ; she uttered a half-audible assent ; the Egyptian rose , and taking her by the hand , he led her across the banquet-room -- the curtains withdrew as by magic hands , and the music broke forth in a louder and gladder strain ; they passed a row of columns , on either side of which fountains cast aloft their fragrant waters ; they descended by broad and easy steps into a garden .
