# text = Arbaces stood before the altar : he had laid his garland on the shrine , and seemed occupied with pouring into the tripod the contents of a brazen vase ; suddenly from that tripod leaped into life a blue , quick , darting , irregular flame ; the Egyptian drew back to the side of Ione , and muttered some words in a language unfamiliar to her ear ; the curtain at the back of the altar waved tremulously to and fro -- it parted slowly , and in the aperture which was thus made , Ione beheld an indistinct and pale landscape , which gradually grew brighter and clearer as she gazed ; at length she discovered plainly trees , and rivers , and meadows , and all the beautiful diversity of the richest earth .
