# text = Wrapped in a pallium that partially concealed his sacred robes , the young Apaecides surveyed the disciple of that new and mysterious creed , to which at one time he had been half a convert Olinthus , accustomed to men of all classes , and combining with the enthusiasm of his faith a profound experience of his kind , guessed , perhaps , by the index of the countenance , something of what passed within the breast of the priest .
