# text = This rite performed , Olinthus turned to the congregation said he said one of the assembly ; and Apaecides beheld in the speaker a man still younger than himself , of a countenance equally worn and pallid , of an eye which equally spoke of the restless and fiery operations of a working mind repeated a second voice , and he who thus spoke was in the prime of manhood ; his bronzed skin and Asiatic features bespoke him a son of Syria -- he had been a robber in his youth said a third voice ; and the priest , again turning to regard the speaker , saw an old man with a long grey beard , whom he recognized as a slave to the wealthy Diomed repeated simultaneously the rest -- men who , with two exceptions , were evidently of the inferior ranks .
