# text = And then these bold and fervent men , nursed in vicissitude , beaten by the rough winds of life -- men of mailed and impervious fortitude , ready to affront a world , prepared for torment and armed for death -- men , who presented all imaginable contrast to the weak nerves , the light hearts , the tender fragility of childhood , crowded round the infants , smoothing their rugged brows and composing their bearded lips to kindly and fostering smiles : and then the old man opened the scroll and he taught the infants to repeat after him that beautiful prayer which we still dedicate to the Lord , and still teach to our children ; and then he told them , in simple phrase , of God's love to the young , and how not a sparrow falls but His eye sees it .
