# text = When Glaucus returned to Pompeii , Nydia had told another year of life ; that year , with its sorrows , its loneliness , its trials , had greatly developed her mind and heart ; and when the Athenian drew her unconsciously to his breast , deeming her still in soul as in years a child -- when he kissed her smooth cheek , and wound his arm round her trembling frame , Nydia felt suddenly , and as by revelation , that those feelings she had long and innocently cherished were of love .
