# text = My father was amongst a mighty crowd that gathered on one of our immemorial hills to hear this sage of the East expound : through the wide throng there rang not a single murmur !-- the jest and the roar , with which our native orators are received , were hushed for him -- and when on the loftiest summit of that hill , raised above the breathless crowd below , stood this mysterious visitor , his mien and his countenance awed every heart , even before a sound left his lips .
