# text = He was a man , I have heard my father say , of no tall stature , but of noble and impressive mien ; his robes were dark and ample ; the declining sun , for it was evening , shone aslant upon his form as it rose aloft , motionless , and commanding ; his countenance was much worn and marked , as of one who had braved alike misfortune and the sternest vicissitude of many climes ; but his eyes were bright with an almost unearthly fire ; and when he raised his arm to speak , it was with the majesty of a man into whom the Spirit of a God hath rushed !
