# text = His first impulse was to throw himself on his son's breast -- his next to start away to wring his hands ; and in the attempt to reprove , his broken voice lost itself in weeping resumed Lydon said the slave sighed the old man , more and more affected by the virtue of his son , but not less strongly convinced of the criminality of his purpose answered the gladiator , gaily As Lydon thus spoke , he had already quitted the dark chamber of his father ; and speaking eagerly , though in a whispered tone , they now stood at the same place in which we introduced the porter at his post said Medon , fervently
