# text = I dare not trust to mere strangers to guide me ; the reputation of women of my rank is easily tarnished -- and though I care not who knows that I love Glaucus , I would not have it imagined that I obtained his love by a spell said the Egyptian , rising and walking ( as if to try his strength ) across the chamber , but with irregular and feeble steps said the Egyptian , impetuously said the Egyptian , with eyes flashing such fierce joy , that Julia's gaze sank trembling beneath them returned the purse-proud Julia added Julia , filling up the incompleted sentence replied Arbaces ; and Julia , half frightened at this unhallowed appointment , but urged on by jealousy and the pique of rivalship , even more than love , resolved to fulfill it .
