# text = At that time , various carriages were in use among the Romans ; the one most used by the richer citizens , when they required no companion in their excursion , was the biga , already described in the early portion of this work ; that appropriated to the matrons , was termed carpentum , which had commonly two wheels ; the ancients used also a sort of litter , a vast sedan-chair , more commodiously arranged than the modern , inasmuch as the occupant thereof could lie down at ease , instead of being perpendicularly and stiffly jostled up and down .
