# text = Sometimes the blaze lingered over the iron-grey heaps of scoria , covered in part with ancient mosses or stunted trees , as if seeking in vain for some gentler product of earth , more worthy of its ire ; and sometimes leaving the whole of that part of the scene in darkness , the lightning , broad and sheeted , hung redly over the ocean , tossing far below , until its waves seemed glowing into fire ; and so intense was the blaze , that it brought vividly into view even the sharp outline of the more distant windings of the bay , from the eternal Misenum , with its lofty brow , to the beautiful Sorrentum and the giant hills behind .
