# text = It was now Ione's turn to pray against the unpleasing prophecy said she returned the hag , quickly With these words she sank again into a stillness profound and fearful , as if the cessation of life itself said Glaucus , after a pause , feeling uncomfortably oppressed beneath a silence so appalling replied the hag , pointing her bony finger to the earth said Glaucus asked the Athenian replied the sorceress , with a ghastly grin ; ' my trade is to give hope to the hopeless : for the crossed in love I have philtres ; for the avaricious , promises of treasure ; for the malicious , potions of revenge ; for the happy and the good , I have only what life has -- curses !
