# text = The fox regarded them from his corner with his keen and fiery eye : and as Glaucus now turned towards the witch , he perceived for the first time , just under her seat , the bright gaze and crested head of a large snake : whether it was that the vivid coloring of the Athenian's cloak , thrown over the shoulders of Ione , attracted the reptile's anger -- its crest began to glow and rise , as if menacing and preparing itself to spring upon the Neapolitan --
