# text = The sectarian sternness which confined virtue and heaven to a chosen few , which saw demons in other gods , and the penalties of hell in other religions -- made the believer naturally anxious to convert all to whom he felt the ties of human affection ; and the circle thus traced by benevolence to man was yet more widened by a desire for the glory of God .
