# text = But the whole heart of that divine old man was bathed in love ; the smile of the Deity had burned away from it the leaven of earthlier and coarser passions , and left to the energy of the hero all the meekness of the child said he , rising at length , as the sun's last ray died in the west With these words the old man pressed Apaecides to his breast , and taking up his staff and scrip , the dog bounded cheerily before him , and with slow steps and downcast eyes he went his way .
