# text = Presently the tall figure of Arbaces , in his way to the house of Diomed , entered the extreme end of the grove ; and at the same instant Apaecides , also bound to his appointment with Olinthus , crossed the Egyptian's path said Arbaces , recognizing the priest at a glance Apaecides started at the voice of the Egyptian ; and halting abruptly , gazed upon him with a countenance full of contending , bitter , and scornful emotions said he at length said Arbaces , in a very low voice -- but his pride , which in that descendant of kings was great , betrayed the wound it received from the insulting epithets of the priest in the quiver of his lip and the flush of his tawny brow The flush on the Egyptian's brow was succeeded by a livid paleness .
