# text = The centurion pressed forward again Olinthus remained silent -- the Egyptian laughed contemptuously added a female voice in the centre of the crowd resumed the soldier , unmoved by the cries around cried the crowd continued the Christian , raising his voice And as he spoke he strode across to the fane , and ere any of the bystanders were aware of his purpose , he , in his compassion or his zeal , struck the statue of wood from its pedestal cried he Further words were denied to him : so gross and daring a sacrilege -- of one , too , of the most sacred of their places of worship -- filled even the most lukewarm with rage and horror .
