# text = But not for Arbaces were such dreams said he , touching the figure with his foot Ha ! who art thou cried the form , in a sharp tone , and as she raised herself from the ground , the starlight fell full on the pale face and fixed but sightless eyes of Nydia the Thessalian said Nydia , in a low voice , ' thou art Arbaces the Egyptian ': then , as if inspired by some sudden impulse , she flung herself at his feet , and clasping his knees , exclaimed , in a wild and passionate tone , ' Oh dread and potent man ! save him -- save him !
