# text = It was among the loveliest customs of the ancients to bury the young at the morning twilight ; for , as they strove to give the softest interpretation to death , so they poetically imagined that Aurora , who loved the young , had stolen them to her embrace ; and though in the instance of the murdered priest this fable could not appropriately cheat the fancy , the general custom was still preserved .
