# text = For if , when he judged her merely the accomplice of Julia in obtaining the philtre , he had felt it was dangerous to the full success of his vengeance to allow her to be at large -- to appear , perhaps , as a witness -- to avow the manner in which the sense of Glaucus had been darkened , and thus win indulgence to the crime of which he was accused -- how much more was she likely to volunteer her testimony when she herself had administered the draught , and , inspired by love , would be only anxious , at any expense of shame , to retrieve her error and preserve her beloved ?
