# text = He had sought Julia ; he had detailed to her the confession of Nydia ; he had easily , therefore , lulled any scruple of conscience which might have led her to extenuate the offence of Glaucus by avowing her share in his frenzy : and the more readily , for her vain heart had loved the fame and the prosperity of Glaucus -- not Glaucus himself , she felt no affection for a disgraced man -- nay , she almost rejoiced in the disgrace that humbled the hated Ione .
