# text = He awoke -- he collected himself -- he blessed the gods whom he disbelieved , that he was in a dream -- he turned his eyes from side to side -- he saw the dawning light break through his small but lofty window -- he was in the Precincts of Day -- he rejoiced -- he smiled ; his eyes fell , and opposite to him he beheld the ghastly features , the lifeless eye , the livid lip -- of the hag of Vesuvius he cried , placing his hands before his eyes , as to shut out the grisly vision
