# text = Still , it was an awful and imposing spectacle , with which modern times have , happily , nothing to compare -- a vast theatre , rising row upon row , and swarming with human beings , from fifteen to eighteen thousand in number , intent upon no fictitious representation -- no tragedy of the stage -- but the actual victory or defeat , the exultant life or the bloody death , of each and all who entered the arena !
